From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Ledda <leonardoledda@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_fg: fix the charging status

The battery shows "Discharging" while it charges.

The charger lookup used the property name as power supply name, so it
never found the charger. Look it up by the power-supplies reference.

The current-based fallback used the PMIC sign, but get_current()
reports a charging battery as positive since the current inversion.

---
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
index f248fee..c3216dd 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
@@ -915,9 +915,10 @@ static int qcom_fg_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN;
 				break;
 			}
-			if (temp < 0)
+			/* get_current() reports a charging battery as positive */
+			if (temp > 0)
 				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
-			else if (temp > 0)
+			else if (temp < 0)
 				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
 			else
 				val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
@@ -1315,10 +1316,14 @@ static int qcom_fg_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 
 	/* Optional: Get charger power supply for status checking */
-	chip->chg_psy = power_supply_get_by_name("power-supplies");
+	chip->chg_psy = power_supply_get_by_reference(dev_fwnode(&pdev->dev), "power-supplies");
+	if (!chip->chg_psy)
+		/* The charger is in the device tree, but not registered yet */
+		return -EPROBE_DEFER;
 	if (IS_ERR(chip->chg_psy)) {
 		ret = PTR_ERR(chip->chg_psy);
-		dev_warn(chip->dev, "Failed to get charger supply: %d\n", ret);
+		if (ret != -ENOENT)
+			dev_warn(chip->dev, "Failed to get charger supply: %d\n", ret);
 		chip->chg_psy = NULL;
 	}
 
